course: dictionary
lesson: 7521
title: Practical: real, useful, hands-on
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Practical is about real things you can do with your hands, not only ideas. «A simple practical fix can end them» means a simple fix that really works. So practical here means useful and sensible.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Igor Sikorsky built the first practical mass-produced helicopters» makes sense if practical means useful and really working, because a helicopter that only worked on paper would not be built in large numbers.
explain: Practical has other jobs too. In science, a practical is a lesson where you do experiments (this is mainly a UK word). A practical person is good at making things work, even when others are stuck on the ideas.
fact: Practical means to do with real things, not only ideas or theory.
fact: A practical person is good at dealing with real problems and making things work.
fact: «Practical work» in science means hands-on testing, where you try things out.
fact: A practical joke is a trick played on someone, and a practical gift is useful, like warm gloves.
fact: Igor Sikorsky, born in Kyiv, built the first practical mass-produced helicopters, the VS-300 and R-4, in the USA. Others built earlier rotorcraft.
exercise: «A simple practical fix can end the argument.» What does practical mean here? | Expensive and difficult | Full of ideas and theory only | Silly and playful | *Useful and sensible, something that works
exercise: In science, what is a practical? | A lesson about the history of rivers | *A lesson where you do experiments | A quiet test with a pencil
exercise: Which gift is practical? | *A useful gift, like warm gloves | A gift that goes missing | A gift that only looks nice on a shelf | A gift you can only read about
test: «He was more practical than academic, good at fixing things.» What does more practical than academic mean? | Quiet and shy | *Good at doing things with his hands, not only books | Good at books but bad at everything else | Very old and wise
test: «Her practical joke made everyone laugh.» What is a practical joke? | *A trick played on someone | A long and boring story | A useful tool for the kitchen | A serious lesson in school
exam: What does practical mean in «the first practical mass-produced helicopters»? | Painted in bright colours | Very small and light | *Useful and really working, able to be made in large numbers | Made only as a drawing
